\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Rescue the perishing, care for 
\par the dying,
\par Snatch them in pity from sin
\par and the grave,
\par Weep o'er the erring one, lift up the fallen,
\par Tell them of Jesus, the mighty to save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Rescue the perishing, care for the dying;
\par Jesus is merciful, Jesus will save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Through they are slighting Him,
\par still He is waiting,
\par Waiting the penitent child to receive,
\par Plead with them earnestly, plead with
\par them gently:
\par He will forgive if they only believe.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Rescue the perishing, care for the dying;
\par Jesus is merciful, Jesus will save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Down in the human heart, crushed 
\par by the tempter,
\par Feelings lie buried that grace 
\par can restore;
\par Touched by a loving hand, wakened by kindness,
\par Chords that were broken will vibrate once more.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Rescue the perishing, care for the dying;
\par Jesus is merciful, Jesus will save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Rescue the perishing- duty 
\par demands it;
\par Strength for Thy labour the Lord 
\par will provide;
\par Back to the narrow way patiently win them;
\par Tell the poor wanderer a Saviour has died.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Rescue the perishing, care for the dying;
\par Jesus is merciful, Jesus will save.
\par \f1 
